WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.267
-Oh, everybody's saying it.
Congratulations.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.734
I'm so happy for you.

00:00:03.734 --> 00:00:05.334
Best movie of the year.
Okay, I'll stop.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:08.000
Let's get down to business.
-It's well-deserved.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.467
It is a great movie and I'm glad

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.734
everybody's bringing it up
because, you know,

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.133
Questlove kind of got cheated
out of some attention there

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.934
at the Oscars.
-I know.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.634
It's like I thought that was
going to be, you know --

00:00:17.634 --> 00:00:20.634
Well, it was a pretty memorable
moment, for a lot of reasons.

00:00:20.634 --> 00:00:22.868
-It was, indeed.
-But I'm so happy for you.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.100
And it's so great to meet you.
-And we are happy for you

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.133
and I think I speak
for Questlove when I say that

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.601
because your show is,
first of all, just picked up

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:31.534
for a second season.
-That's correct.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:34.167
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.000
[ Laughs ]
-A really great show.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.534
-Thank you.
-Funny and moving

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:40.167
and all of those things
you would want from a show.

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:43.234
And the show is set,
for those who don't know,

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.734
in your actual hometown,
Manhattan, Kansas.

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.234
Did you shoot it
in your hometown?

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.200
-Well, we shot
a little bit there.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.734
We shot some outside of Chicago,

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.601
but it's Manhattan, Kansas,
the Little Apple.

00:00:51.601 --> 00:00:52.801
If you haven't been,
you got to go.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.100
Stop by Varsity Donuts.
It's a really good time.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.567
-Did they just call it
the Little Apple

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.267
or is there
some representation of --

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:00.634
-Oh, it's called that.
There's like, you know,

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.534
like a big water tower
with an apple on it

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:04.033
and there's like
Little Apple Brewery,

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.400
Little Apple this,
Little apple that, so.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.200
-And what college is
in Manhattan, Kansas?

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.868
-Kansas State. Powercats.
-But you did not go
to Kansas State.

00:01:11.868 --> 00:01:13.000
-No, I went to Arizona State.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.501
-And I went
to Arizona State, too.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:15.868
-That's what I heard.
-Yeah.

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:17.334
I don't know
if we overlapped at all.

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.067
I didn't actually go to class,
so that was --

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.234
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.267
-I barely did,
but I studied opera.

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.567
Were you...?
-Same here.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.234
-What were you up to
when you were there?

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.667
What were you doing
like socially?

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:31.167
-Oh, God. Just, you know.
-Where'd you hang out?

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.601
-The Dash.
-The Dash was the big
place then, yeah.

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:36.234
-Yeah. And then Whataburger
on the way home

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.133
and that was pretty much it.

00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:38.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.334
-I learned a special skill
at The Dash,

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:43.601
which was that you don't need
a glass to drink beer out of.

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.467
You can just drink it
right out of the pitcher.

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.467
-That's right. That's right.
And, as a matter of fact,

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.267
I used to be on the swim team --
for like one year --

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:51.467
but you would drink
a whole pitcher of beer

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.801
and then your alarm would go off
at like 5:00 in the morning

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:56.400
and you'd throw up
in the gutter, so, anyway.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.834
It was a different time.

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.000
Now, I just, you know,
throw up anywhere.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.968
It's New York.
-You brought a video for us

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.400
of your mother.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.868
-Who's an interesting woman.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.868 --> 00:02:11.567
-I think maybe we should show
the video first.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:12.667
-Let's get to know her
a little bit.

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:13.767
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, sure.

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:15.100
-Teeny tiny penis.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:15.968
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.267
-What was the teeny tiny penis?

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:19.634
-He had a little [bleep]

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:20.934
-Who?

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.267
-Your father.

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:27.567
But he used it plenty,
believe me.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.100
-With who?

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.067
-With anybody
he could get it in.

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:32.534
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:35.467
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:02:38.534 --> 00:02:40.000
-Dear old dad.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.901
So your mom is not the shy
and reserved type,

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.000
is what I'm guessing.
-Oh,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.834
no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:48.000
We used to go to Food 4 Less,
which was

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.501
a grocery store at the time.
-Yeah. It still is.

00:02:50.501 --> 00:02:51.968
-Yeah.
-Kind of.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:54.367
-She would go in like
her nightgown,

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:55.968
but like just paper thin.

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.367
It'd be like from the '70s

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:58.968
and we're in the late '80s
by now.

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:01.534
And she said these long,
long hanging boobs.

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.300
We called it beaver tails.
And she would just walk.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.701
[ Laughter ]
You know, just didn't give a --

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:09.367
She did not care.

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:10.834
But I think, you know,
in some ways,

00:03:10.834 --> 00:03:12.968
that's kind of what brought me
to this moment right now.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.667
-Oh, inspiration, yeah.

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:17.100
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.567
-Oh, I'm getting hot, Jimmy.

00:03:18.567 --> 00:03:20.501
I'm getting hot.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:22.367
No, I mean, if you see these
without this --

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:23.834
Somebody make a good
plus-size bra

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.400
because, if I took
this thing off,

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.000
they'd be rolling
around my knees and...

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.000
I'd be like mother,
like daughter right now.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.434
Cut this.
Fix this in post.

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:32.734
Cut this whole interview.

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:36.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:38.067
Hi, guys.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.267
Did you stay in Phoenix
after college

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.234
or did you go back home?

00:03:43.234 --> 00:03:45.634
-I did, I stayed in Arizona
for a while.

00:03:45.634 --> 00:03:47.300
I was knocking around
in karaoke bars

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.267
and I was waiting tables

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.534
at P.F. Chang's,
the original one,

00:03:50.534 --> 00:03:53.133
thank you so much.
-Oh, the original, yeah, yeah.

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
-The original one.

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:56.534
In Scottsdale Fashion Square.

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.667
It was a real hot spot

00:03:57.667 --> 00:04:00.601
for like sports celebrities.
-Oh, really?

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:01.400
Like who?
-Oh, you got your, oh, you know,

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.968
your Charles Barkley, of course.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.868
-Oh, he played for the Suns.
-And he was huge at the time

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.100
and he brought in everybody.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.434
Like one night,
I was waiting on him

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:09.968
and Michael Jordan
and Payne Stewart

00:04:09.968 --> 00:04:11.501
and Ahmad Rashad
and all these people.

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:13.834
But one night, he brought in
"The Nature Boy" Ric Flair.

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.067
[ Laughs ]
-The wrestler.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:17.267
The great wrestler, yeah.
-Whoo! Anybody -- Okay.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:20.267
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]
Anyway.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.200
-Some of them are still
holding back tears.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:24.934
-Well, I'm happy you're here.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:27.767
Anyway, The Nature Boy,
I was so excited because like

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.167
I grew up with him
in the household.

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.133
He was like, you know,

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:31.801
my brothers used
to watch wrestling

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.667
and like body slam me and stuff.
It was wonderful.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.400
[ Laughter ]
-He had that beautiful mane

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.601
of blond hair.
-Yeah, showbiz, you know.

00:04:37.601 --> 00:04:39.300
Total wrestler,
like with the outfits.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.534
You got to look him up.
If you don't know

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:42.901
The Nature Boy Ric Flair,
you got to look him up.

00:04:42.901 --> 00:04:44.567
Anyway, I'm sort of going off.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.801
-What did Nature Boy like
to eat?

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:50.901
-Well, Nature Boy,
I don't know what he got up to,

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.033
but I do know Charles Barkley
was my regular,

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:54.400
so he had the pot stickers.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:55.734
He got those.
-Oh, Charles liked
the pot stickers.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.567
-Yeah, yeah.
-Was Charles a good tipper?

00:04:57.567 --> 00:04:59.200
-Charles was a very consistent,
good tipper.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.300
-Oh, yeah.
-Yeah, and there was
a whole range

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.634
with some of those sports stars,
but, yeah,

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:04.901
he was always a good tipper.
-Ooh! Oh, so some of them

00:05:04.901 --> 00:05:06.934
stiffed you, huh?
-No, no, no, no, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.934 --> 00:05:09.601
But he was good.

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:11.133
He would have me sing sometimes.

00:05:11.133 --> 00:05:13.434
Because, if you didn't know,
I'm a singer.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.200
You can look it up on YouTube.
It's everywhere.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.934
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, so, you knew him
really well.

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.901
-Well, enough, you know.
It was kind of like he was --

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.434
Let me just have
a little sip of water.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.367
-Yeah, go ahead.
Enjoy. Go crazy.

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:23.834
-You got to stay hydrated.
It's flu season.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:26.734
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, my point was that

00:05:26.734 --> 00:05:28.100
he brought in
Nature Boy Ric Flair

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.601
and I was so freaked out
because like, to me,

00:05:30.601 --> 00:05:32.868
like he was like, that was like
a movie star, you know,

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:35.734
in the flash and he's like,
"Do you want to sing for him?"

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:37.534
I was like, "I don't know,"
and then so I just --

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.300
He's like, "Come on,
sing for him," but I was scared,

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:41.868
so I sat
on Charles Barkley's lap

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:43.534
[ Laughter ]
and sang and sort of
with my head

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:45.801
like sort of buried in his neck
and I sang

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.934
"I've Got a Crush on You"
to The Nature Boy Ric Flair,

00:05:47.934 --> 00:05:49.400
[ Laughter and applause ]
just one chair over.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.667
And I doubt either one of them
remember that,

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.567
but it was one of the best
moments of my life.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:55.801
-It's a pretty good life moment.
-Yeah.

00:05:55.801 --> 00:05:57.901
-Well, it's great to have
you here.

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.901
-Thank you.
-The show, if you haven't
seen it, it's great.

00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:00.634
It's called
"Somebody Somewhere."

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:02.701
It's on HBO and HBO Max.

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.300
Bridget Everett, everybody.
Thank you, Bridget.

